{"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Two systems give a game its voice: ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText","type":"reference"},{"text":", the table of every stock line the engine can say, and the seeded random stream behind ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/random(_:)","type":"reference"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"oneOf(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/chance(_:)","type":"reference"},{"text":", which lets responses vary without ever varying between replays of the same seed.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Speaking-in-your-own-voice","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Speaking in your own voice"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every standard response — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Taken."},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"You can't go that way."},{"type":"text","text":", the inventory header, the parser’s complaints — lives on a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" value. Override any subset from your game’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" property; everything you don’t touch keeps the classic default:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["struct Snark: Game {","    \/\/ …","","    var text: GameText {","        var text = GameText()","        text.taken = \"Snagged.\"","        text.cantGoThatWay = \"Walls exist, you know.\"","        return text","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every line is a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/Line","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", and a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Line","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" takes a bare string as readily as a closure — so whether a line names the thing it is about, or looks around before it speaks, is the game’s call and not a shape the engine picked:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["text.cantReach = .naming { \"\\($0.sentenceCased) is right there, and yet.\" }","text.pitchBlack = .live { lantern.isOn ? \"Dark, and getting darker.\" : \"Pitch black.\" }"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"What the generic parameter says is what the line is ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"given"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":". A line built around a name takes a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/Noun","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"; one about nothing in particular takes ","type":"text"},{"code":"Void","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and reaches for ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/Line\/live(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" when it wants the turn it prints in rather than the moment it was written. Neither costs a game that wants the plain sentence anything: that spelling is the string literal, in every slot.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Articles are the engine’s job","type":"heading","anchor":"Articles-are-the-engines-job","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A naming line receives a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/Noun","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" — a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"rendered noun phrase","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"code":"the brass lantern","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"a brass lantern","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Mrs. Vane","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") that also knows its own number — never a bare name. The article is chosen before the closure runs, because only the engine knows which entities carry the ","type":"text"},{"code":"properName","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" trait:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let constance = Actor {","    name(\"Mrs. Vane\")","    properName","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"With that one word, every stock line reads correctly: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Mrs. Vane is right here."},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"You see nothing special about Mrs. Vane."},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Mrs. Vane would take exception to that."},{"type":"text","text":" Without it they all say "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"the Mrs. Vane"},{"text":", and a disambiguation between a person and a prop — which has to article one and not the other in the same sentence — could not be fixed by re-skinning at all.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Where a line ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"opens"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" on the phrase, reach for ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/Noun\/sentenceCased","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":": ","type":"text"},{"code":"the troll","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" has to be capitalized and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Mrs. Vane","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" must be left alone.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["text.cantTakeActor = .naming { \"\\($0.sentenceCased) would sooner not.\" }"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The other three helpers are public statics too, for a custom line that builds a phrase of its own: "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/definite(_:proper:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GameText\/indefinite(_:proper:)"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/list(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", which joins already-rendered phrases into an English list. A rule can reach the same forms through "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/definiteName","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/indefiniteName","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A capitalized ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"name(…)"},{"text":" on an item or actor without ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"properName"},{"text":" is a non-fatal bootstrap warning — not an inference, since ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Elvish sword"},{"text":" is a common noun, but the author who meant a proper name shouldn’t have to find out from a transcript. Location names are exempt: the engine never articles a room.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Text a game declares itself (descriptions, rule replies) never goes through ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GameText"},{"type":"text","text":"; it’s already in your voice."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The stub verbs’ stock replies are grouped on ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/stubs","type":"reference"},{"text":" rather than sitting flat alongside the rest, since there are about fifty of them:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["text.stubs.pray = \"No one is listening. You checked.\"","text.stubs.attack = .naming { \"The Institute frowns on assaulting \\($0).\" }","text.stubs.smash = .naming { \"\\($0.sentenceCased) \\($0.verb(\"is\", \"are\")) stouter than your temper.\" }"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Overriding one re-skins the line; replacing the "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"behavior"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is a rule or an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"actions"},{"type":"text","text":" row. See "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/StubVerbs","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Those three are the same type, and it is the same type the lines above use. A verb with no object slot on any row — "},{"code":"sing","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"pray","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"swim","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — is a "},{"code":"Line<Nothing>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Line"},{"type":"text","text":" is handed a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/Noun","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", never a bare name: the rendered phrase plus its number, so "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/Noun\/verb(_:_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" can pick the form that agrees and a game may call a thing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rails"},{"type":"text","text":" and get “The rails are not food.” Interpolating one prints its phrase, so a line with no verb to agree pays nothing for the facility. The number comes from the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plural"},{"text":" trait, declared for the same reason ","type":"text"},{"code":"properName","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is: no engine should guess it, and no game should have to rename a thing to suit a stock line.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A line about "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"several","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" things is a line about one. "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/Noun\/list(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" joins them into a single noun that carries the number the "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"whole phrase"}]},{"type":"text","text":" has — plural when there are several, and also when the only one is itself plural:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["text.inTheContainer = .naming { \"In \\($0.holder) \\($0.item.verb(\"is\", \"are\")) \\($0.item).\" }"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"That second rule is why the helper exists rather than a "},{"code":"[Noun]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" parameter. The engine used to decide by counting, so one plural thing in a box printed “In the hamper is some scales.” — and the rule lived in the line’s body, where a game re-voicing it had to re-derive it and could get it wrong the same way. The template above never counts anything."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/inventorySentence","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" is the exception, over "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/Carried","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":": it has something to say about "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"each","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" thing it lists — which of them is being worn — so it cannot have them joined before the game has had its say."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A line about ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"two","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" things is a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Line","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" too, over a role struct that names them — ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/Holding","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" (a thing and what holds it), "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/Gift","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/Aboard","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["text.putItemIn = .naming { \"You tuck \\($0.item) into \\($0.holder).\" }"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The roles are a type rather than a pair because "},{"code":"\\($0.holder)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" answers the question an author actually asks — which one is the container? — and "},{"code":"\\($1)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" does not. Both halves are nouns, which matters more here than for a one-object line: a two-object sentence has two things its verb might agree with, and it is rarely the one named first. "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/itemOnSurface"},{"type":"text","text":" reads “On the table are the rails.”"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every stock line is a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Line"},{"text":". What differs is its ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"subject"}]},{"text":" — the type it is about — and the set of those is the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/LineSubject"},{"text":" protocol rather than a list somebody has to keep current: ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/Nothing"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/Noun"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Noun?"},{"text":", the role structs above, and five more for the lines about something that isn’t in the world at all. A word quoted back at the player is a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/Word"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/unknownWord"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/noReferent"},{"text":"); the part of a sentence the parser is still waiting for is a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/Prompt"},{"text":" (the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"missing…"},{"type":"text","text":" family); the things one phrase matched are "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/Choices"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/ambiguous"},{"type":"text","text":"); the title is a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/Banner-swift.struct"},{"type":"text","text":" and the score a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/Score"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Those last five are the ones a line may ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" leave unsaid, and the type enforces it. ","type":"text"},{"code":"Line","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"ExpressibleByStringLiteral","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" only where its subject conforms to ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/DroppableSubject","type":"reference"},{"text":", so a fixed sentence is available to every line about a thing in the world — ","type":"text"},{"code":"text.putItemIn = \"Done.\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" prints no names and is still true — and unavailable where the subject ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"is"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" the content:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["text.unknownWord = \"Eh?\"                                    \/\/ does not compile","text.unknownWord = .naming { \"There is no \\\"\\($0)\\\" here.\" } \/\/ the only way to write it"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A line handed ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"nothing","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" has nothing to drop, which is why ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/pitchBlack","isActive":true},{"text":" is a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Line<Nothing>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and takes a literal like the rest.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"Randomness-that-replays","type":"heading","text":"Randomness that replays"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Rule bodies can vary their behavior with three helpers:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["thief.before(.examine) {","    try reply(oneOf(","        \"The thief eyes you with polite menace.\",","        \"The thief pretends not to notice you.\",","    ))","}","","world.afterEachTurn {","    if chance(5) {","        say(\"Somewhere below, something skitters.\")","    }","}","","let damage = random(2...12)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"All three draw from one stream whose position lives in the world state. That buys two guarantees:","type":"text"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Replays"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": a world built with ","type":"text"},{"code":"GameWorld\/init(game:seed:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" plays out identically for the same seed and commands, on every platform — the backbone of transcript tests and reproducible bug reports. The plain ","type":"text"},{"code":"GameWorld\/init(game:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" seeds fresh each run.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Saves","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": the stream’s position is part of the saved state, so a restored game continues with exactly the randomness it would have had.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Pin the seed in a test the same way the engine’s own suite does:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let world = try GameWorld(game: MyGame(), seed: 42)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"anchor":"See-also","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"See also"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WritingRules"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TextAndRandomness","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/gnusto\/textandrandomness"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Text and Randomness","anchor":"Text-and-Randomness","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/Line","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/StubReplies","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/random(_:)","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/chance(_:)"]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Gnusto"}],"title":"Text and Randomness"},"abstract":[{"text":"Re-skin the engine’s stock lines, and roll dice that replay.","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/GameText/unknownWord":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/gametext\/unknownword","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/unknownWord","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A word outside the game’s whole vocabulary.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"unknownWord","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"unknownWord"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"GameText","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8GameTextV"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Line","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8GameTextV4LineV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"GameText","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8GameTextV"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Word","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8GameTextV4WordV"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}]},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/GameText/stubs":{"fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"stubs","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8GameTextV","text":"GameText","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8GameTextV11StubRepliesV","text":"StubReplies","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/stubs","title":"stubs","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The stock replies for the verbs the parser knows as words but the engine"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"gives no mechanic. Re-skin one with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"text.stubs.dig = \"…\""},{"type":"text","text":"; give one real"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"behavior with a rule or an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"actions"},{"type":"text","text":" row."}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/gametext\/stubs"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/GameText":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"GameText"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Every stock player-facing line the engine can say, as one overridable","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"value — so a game can speak in its own voice without touching behavior."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"GameText","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/gametext","title":"GameText","type":"topic"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/GameText/Choices":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/Choices","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/gametext\/choices","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The things one noun phrase turned out to match."}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Choices","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"GameText.Choices","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Choices","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/random(_:)":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"random"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SN","text":"ClosedRange"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":">) -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/random(_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/random(_:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A uniform draw from t